## Excel Export Logic

### Template
- File: `templates/Monthly_Worklog_Template.xlsx`
- **Critical sheet: `empty`** — this is the standard template for every month sheet
  - Headers at row 4
  - Data starts at row 5 (`data_start = 5`)
  - 997 pre-styled rows (rows 5–1001) (`template_rows = 997`)
- `Dashboard` sheet: filled with member name, department, staff_id, position, year

### Column mapping (data rows)
| Column | Content |
|---|---|
| A (1) | Date (`dd/mm/yyyy`) — only on first entry of each day |
| B (2) | Project name |
| C (3) | Task |
| D (4) | Start time (`h:mm`) |
| E (5) | End time (`h:mm`) |
| F (6) | Hours (float) |
| G (7) | Status |
| H (8) | Note |

### Generation flow (`generate_excel_bytes`)
1. Query all worklogs for the member+year
2. Build `by_month_day[(month, day)] = [entries...]`
3. Load template workbook
4. Fill Dashboard sheet
5. Delete all old named month sheets (January–December) if present
6. For each selected month: `wb.copy_worksheet(ws_empty)`, title = month name
7. Build `row_data` — **only days with actual entries** (no blank day rows)
   - First entry of a day: `(date_obj, entry)`
   - Additional entries same day: `(None, entry)`
8. Insert extra rows only if entries exceed 997 (copy style from last template row)
9. Delete `empty` sheet from output
10. Fill `tbl_project` / `Config` sheets with current project names

### Month filter
- API param: `months=1,3,6,12` (comma-separated integers)
- If omitted or empty: generates all 12 months
- Frontend: month filter modal opens before download, all months checked by default

